---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
// How SCiEL works: one step inside a deme (four stations), and culture between demes.
// The bold part names are exactly the parts switched off in the ablation (methods.ts).
// src/figures/framework.ts opens a small working demo of the step a reader taps.
---
<Figure width="wide">
  <div class="fw" id="fw">
    <p class="fw-lab">Inside each deme: one step, repeated <span>Tap a step to see it work</span></p>
    <ol class="fw-steps">
      <li tabindex="0" role="button" data-s="0"><span class="fw-n">1</span><b>Choose</b>
        <svg class="fw-ico" viewBox="0 0 96 52" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="4" y1="46" x2="92" y2="46" style="stroke:var(--rule)"/>
          <circle cx="14" cy="38" r="3.5" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="32" cy="32" r="5" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="52" cy="36" r="4" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="74" cy="24" r="7" fill="#D0702F"/>
          <circle cx="74" cy="24" r="12" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-ink)" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <path d="M74 2v7m-3.5-3.5 3.5 3.5 3.5-3.5" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-ink)" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        </svg>
        <p>The <strong>learned policy</strong> picks a parent and an edit.</p></li>
      <li tabindex="0" role="button" data-s="1"><span class="fw-n">2</span><b>Screen</b>
        <svg class="fw-ico" viewBox="0 0 96 52" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="4" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.3"/><circle cx="10" cy="26" r="4" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.3"/><circle cx="10" cy="42" r="4" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <path d="M15 10h22M15 42h22" style="stroke:var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
          <path d="M37 6l8 8m0-8l-8 8M37 38l8 8m0-8l-8 8" style="stroke:var(--fig-down)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M52 2v18M52 32v18" style="stroke:var(--fig-ink)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          <path d="M15 26h63" style="stroke:var(--fig-ink)" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <circle cx="83" cy="26" r="5" fill="#D0702F"/>
        </svg>
        <p>The <strong>world model</strong> skips likely failures.</p></li>
      <li tabindex="0" role="button" data-s="2"><span class="fw-n">3</span><b>Write and test</b>
        <svg class="fw-ico" viewBox="0 0 96 52" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="4" y="6" width="50" height="40" rx="3" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--rule-strong)"/>
          <path d="M11 15h30M11 23h22" style="stroke:var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M11 31h34" style="stroke:var(--fig-up)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M11 39h18" style="stroke:var(--fig-down)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" opacity=".55"/>
          <path d="M58 26h8" style="stroke:var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.3"/>
          <circle cx="80" cy="26" r="12" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-up)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M74 26.5l4 4 8-8.5" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-up)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
        <p>The model edits the code; a checker scores it.</p></li>
      <li tabindex="0" role="button" data-s="3"><span class="fw-n">4</span><b>Keep and log</b>
        <svg class="fw-ico" viewBox="0 0 96 52" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="30" r="4" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="24" cy="18" r="4.5" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="26" cy="38" r="3.5" fill="#D0702F"/>
          <circle cx="40" cy="26" r="6.5" fill="#D0702F"/><circle cx="40" cy="26" r="11" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-ink)" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <rect x="62" y="6" width="30" height="40" rx="3" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--rule-strong)"/>
          <path d="M68 15h18M68 23h18M68 31h18M68 39h11" style="stroke:var(--rule-strong)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
        <p>Better programs stay; every choice is logged.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="fw-panel" id="fw-panel" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <p class="fw-back">↺ repeat, in every deme at once</p>

    <p class="fw-lab" style="margin-top:28px">Between demes: culture</p>
    <p class="fw-flow">A <strong class="term" tabindex="0" data-def="A question a deme keeps open: it plans an experiment, writes a tool, runs it, concludes.">research cell</strong> tests a hunch; what holds becomes a <em class="term" tabindex="0" data-def="A research cell's conclusion, with its measured effect.">finding</em> that other demes try.</p>
    <svg class="fw-lane" viewBox="0 -12 620 196" role="img" aria-label="A finding from Deme 1 helps in Deme 2 and is kept; it does not help in Deme 3 and is dropped">
      <path class="fw-arc" d="M164 82 Q300 14 437 30" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-chord)" stroke-width="2" />
      <path class="fw-arc2" d="M164 96 Q300 164 437 148" fill="none" style="stroke:var(--fig-chord)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="6 6" />
      <text x="300" y="20" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--fig-chord)">kept: it helped</text>
      <text x="300" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--muted)">dropped: it did not</text>
      <circle cx="150" cy="89" r="13" fill="#D0702F" />
      <circle cx="450" cy="30" r="13" fill="#3A6EA5" />
      <circle cx="450" cy="148" r="13" fill="#B08A20" />
      <text x="128" y="94" text-anchor="end" style="fill:var(--ink)">Deme 1</text>
      <text x="472" y="35" style="fill:var(--ink)">Deme 2</text>
      <text x="472" y="153" style="fill:var(--ink)">Deme 3</text>
    </svg>

  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Figure 2.</b> How SCiEL works. The parts in bold are the ones switched off, one at a time, in Figure 6;
    red lines mean the same as in Figure 1.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
